$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ DP600 single-element uniaxial tension  --  MSC Nastran SOL 400
$
$   units : mm - N - tonne - s   (stress MPa, density 7.85-9)
$   model : 1 x 1 x 1 mm CHEXA, 1/8 symmetry, x-face pulled to u = 0.5 mm
$   check : sigma_x ~= 700.3 MPa at the end (see README.md)
$
$   WHY SOL 400 AND NOT SOL 106:
$     this deck stretches the element to 40% true strain.  SOL 106 offers large
$     DISPLACEMENT (PARAM,LGDISP) but not large STRAIN for plasticity, so it is
$     outside its validity here.  SOL 400 adds large strain, and the guide lists
$     it as a separate trigger: "Large displacement by LGDISP parameter ...
$     Large strain by LRGSTRN".  Both are switched on below.
$
$   Large strain also needs the "advanced" element: the traditional PSOLID must
$   be supplemented by PSLDN1 (BEH=SOLID).  PSOLID alone silently stays on the
$   older formulation.
$
$   NOTE the table convention: TABLES1 under MATS1 is stress vs TOTAL strain,
$   first point at the ORIGIN and the SECOND point at the yield point named in
$   LIMIT1.  This is NOT the same table as Abaqus/Ansys/LS-DYNA use.
$-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SOL 400
CEND
TITLE    = DP600 1-element tension (mm-N-tonne-s)
ECHO     = NONE
$
SUBCASE 1
  LABEL = pull x face to 0.5 mm
  ANALYSIS     = NLSTATICS
  SPC          = 1
  LOAD         = 2
  NLPARM       = 10
  DISPLACEMENT(PLOT) = ALL
  STRESS(PLOT)       = ALL
  STRAIN(PLOT)       = ALL
  SPCFORCES(PLOT)    = ALL
$
BEGIN BULK
$
PARAM,LGDISP,1
PARAM,POST,-1
NLMOPTS,LRGSTRN,1
$
$       ID      NINC    DT      KMETHOD KSTEP   MAXITER CONV    INTOUT
$ SOL 400 with NLPARM requires KMETHOD=FNT (full Newton, stiffness updated
$ every iteration).  AUTO/SEMI/ITER are the SOL 106-era strategies.
NLPARM  10      50              FNT     5       25      PW      YES
$
$===============================================================================
$ MESH
$===============================================================================
$       ID                      X       Y       Z
GRID    1               0.0     0.0     0.0
GRID    2               1.0     0.0     0.0
GRID    3               1.0     1.0     0.0
GRID    4               0.0     1.0     0.0
GRID    5               0.0     0.0     1.0
GRID    6               1.0     0.0     1.0
GRID    7               1.0     1.0     1.0
GRID    8               0.0     1.0     1.0
$
$       EID     PID     G1      G2      G3      G4      G5      G6
CHEXA   1       1       1       2       3       4       5       6
+       7       8
$
$       PID     MID     CORDM
PSOLID  1       1       0
$ advanced (large strain) solid: C8 = 8-node hex, BEH = SOLID, INT = L
PSLDN1  1       1
+       C8      SOLID   L
$
$===============================================================================
$ MATERIAL
$===============================================================================
$       MID     E       G       NU      RHO
MAT1    1       210000.         0.3     7.85-9
$
$       MID     TID     TYPE    H       YF      HR      LIMIT1  LIMIT2
MATS1   1       200     PLASTIC         1       1       350.0
$
$ stress vs TOTAL strain.  second point 350/210000 = 0.00167 must agree with
$ both LIMIT1 (350.) and the MAT1 Young's modulus, or the initial stiffness is
$ defined twice and convergence suffers.
$ stress vs TOTAL strain.  8-character fields, so the values butt up against
$ each other -- that is normal fixed format, not a typo.  Pairs are:
$   (0, 0) (.0016667, 350) (.0221667, 455) (.1026667, 560)
$   (.4033333, 700) (1.003761, 790)
$ The second point reproduces the elastic slope of MAT1: 350/.0016667 = 210000.
TABLES1 200
+       .0000000.0000000.0016667350.0000.0221667455.0000.1026667560.0000
+       .4033333700.00001.003761790.0000
+       ENDT
$
$===============================================================================
$ BOUNDARY CONDITIONS   (1/8 symmetry + enforced displacement)
$   The pulled DOF must be in the SPC set; SPCD supplies its value and the
$   subcase must select that SPCD set through LOAD.
$===============================================================================
$       SID     C       G1      G2      G3      G4
SPC1    1       1       1       4       5       8
SPC1    1       2       1       2       5       6
SPC1    1       3       1       2       3       4
SPC1    1       1       2       3       6       7
$
$       SID     G1      C1      D1      G2      C2      D2
SPCD    2       2       1       0.5     3       1       0.5
SPCD    2       6       1       0.5     7       1       0.5
$
ENDDATA
